Additional company profile findings
The live company profile also contains the Vijay Gupta biography and 2025 award claim described above, so those are not exclusive to the competing preview. Its stated values cover integrity, excellence, teamwork, customer focus, sustainability, safety and respect; elsewhere it uses ethics, perfection, innovation, harmony and safety. Mission and vision prose emphasize dependable alloy supply, manufacturing capability, employee development, customer trust and social responsibility. The establishment year counter extracted as zero and cannot support a founding date.
Additional sustainability findings
The sustainability page claims 83 MW of solar power and 29.6 MW of installed wind capacity. It describes a Ghatsila, Jharkhand expansion with two 1,000 TPD sponge iron plants, a planned 90 MW waste heat recovery power plant and existing 24 MVA furnace operations. Biomass is described as an option under exploration. The 83 MW claim and the homepage 2.6 MW project may refer to different scopes or stages; the website does not reconcile them. Do not combine them into a total.
Its editorial discussion links low carbon ferro alloys with green steelmaking, emissions, energy efficiency and ESG goals. These are website assertions rather than a verified life cycle assessment; product carbon content alone does not demonstrate a lower manufacturing carbon footprint.
