Careers and form fields
The careers page describes collaboration, innovation, work and life balance, rewards, practical training, workshops, progression, mentorship, inclusive recruitment, equal opportunity, occupational safety, health checks and employee celebrations.
An Administration and Facilities Manager role in Visakhapatnam requests a B.Com, BBA, B.Sc or equivalent qualification and 2–5 years of experience. Tasks cover facilities, housekeeping, security, vendors, office supplies, travel, expense control and administrative records. Excel, Word, communication and negotiation skills are requested.
An MIS Executive role lists head office Kolkata and Dhalbhumgarh or Ghatsila locations, equivalent graduate qualifications and 2–4 years of plant or factory MIS experience. Work includes goods receipt and issue entries, shift reporting, production and dispatch logs, stock reconciliation, cross department coordination and SAP entries following training. Prior SAP experience is not required; Excel proficiency is emphasized. Vacancy status needs confirmation.
The general application form requests name, mobile, email, department and CV. Departments listed are production, quality assurance, quality control, purchase, sales and marketing, finance, administration, HR, engineering, research and development, and IT. General CV upload allows PDF, DOCX, JPG and PNG up to 10 MB; the role specific form shows 5 MB and additionally asks for the role. Contact form fields are name, email, phone, subject and message. Product enquiry forms request name, email, mobile, product and message. Brochure and analysis report actions appear on product pages; successful downloads and submissions were not tested.
Product uses and process information
The product pages describe ferro manganese as a steel alloying and deoxidising input used in construction, vehicles, railways and engineering. They attribute strength, hardness, toughness and wear resistance benefits to it. High carbon production is described through smelting, refining and casting; low carbon material is associated with AOD purification. The site claims 80–93 percent less carbon addition for medium or low carbon FeMn compared with high carbon FeMn; validate the comparison before reuse.
Silico manganese is described as an iron, silicon and manganese alloy used for combined deoxidation and alloying. Applications include alloy, carbon, tool and stainless steels, with medium and low carbon grades associated with 200 series stainless steel, foundries and electrode coatings. The site claims 4–6 percent productivity improvements during decarburisation and improved furnace lining life. Its category FAQ gives typical Mn 60–70 percent, Si 12–18 percent and C 1.5–2.5 percent, qualified by grade and application.
Ferro chrome is presented as a chromium source for stainless and specialty steels, improving corrosion, heat and wear resistance. The FAQ gives typical high carbon composition Cr 50–70 percent and C 6–8 percent, with iron as balance. Low carbon production is described using silicothermic reduction and optional vacuum treatment; example applications include 304L and 316L stainless steels, superalloys and chemical equipment.
Ferro silicon applications listed include carbon and alloy steels, stainless steel, cast iron, electrical steel, motor and transformer cores, and corrosion or heat resistant ferrous alloys. The page calls silicon an oxidant; technical wording should be reviewed before publishing.
